2. Compute 24-month mean & anomaly multiples: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales, then compute the ratio = month_sales / 24-month_mean for every month. Identify the top-3 (region, product_line, month) combinations with the highest ratio. Also extract the return_rate for those specific months. Save intermediate results to a CSV file. → code_agent
3. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For the top-3 anomaly combinations, analyze surrounding months (3 months before and after) to check if the spike is isolated (suggesting channel stuffing) or part of a sustained trend (suggesting real demand). Also compare return_rate of the spike month vs the 24-month average return_rate. Save analysis results to a CSV. → code_agent
